# v29 (2026-09-10) -- THE PATENT AND GLAFKIDES HARVEST. Nineteen fields.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⚠ THE LARGEST BUMP IN THIS LOG, AND EVERY FIELD IN IT IS INERT AT THE
# SHIPPED DEFAULT. All 184 film profiles and all 11 print stocks render
# bit-identically to a v28 database; `verify.py` asserts it (G-V29-INERT).
# The bump is a truth claim about the SHAPE of the record, and specifically
# about a class of error the schema could not previously express.
#
# WHERE IT CAME FROM. 41 documents read in full on 2026-09-10: 34 patents
# (CN, EP, RU, US, 1941-2002), one MSc thesis, and both volumes of Pierre
# Glafkides, «Photographic Chemistry» -- 1022 pages of textbook, which is the
# first source in this project's corpus that states LAWS and PER-CLASS
# CONSTANTS rather than per-product measurements. 564 findings. One document
# (US2249541, 1941) carried nothing usable and that is recorded as a
# content-based judgement, not a title-based one.
#
# THE ORGANISING OBSERVATION, which is why these nineteen fields and not
# others: THIS SCHEMA HAS BEEN STORING MEASUREMENTS WITHOUT STORING WHAT WAS
# MEASURED. Six of the nineteen exist purely to attach a definition to a
# number that was already there --
#
#   GrainSpec.rms_aperture_um        an rms with no aperture is not a figure.
#                                    Kodak read 48 um, Konica 25 um; treating
#                                    the two as comparable overstates Konica
#                                    grain by 39 %, which is more than the
#                                    whole spread between a 100 and a 400
#                                    speed stock.
#   DyeImpurity.measurement_mode     the magenta unwanted-blue absorption came
#                                    back as 0.137/0.048 from one patent and
#                                    0.36/0.20 from two others. NEITHER IS
#                                    WRONG: the first is transmission on film,
#                                    the second reflection on paper. Averaging
#                                    them would have produced a `dye_matrix`
#                                    describing no real material.
#   FilmProfile.gamma_criterion      nine incompatible definitions of "gamma"
#                                    in 41 documents.
#   FilmProfile.density_geometry     `callier_q` is a ratio between two of
#                                    four densities and never said which two.
#   MTFSpec.turbidity_ref_log_e      the exposure at which the stored f50 was
#                                    read, so switching turbidity on cannot
#                                    silently move the mid-scale.
#   CoatingSpec.coverage_source      a coating weight is unreadable unless it
#                                    says whether the silver-halide-to-metal
#                                    conversion was applied.
#
# The other thirteen carry physics the pipeline had no representation for:
#
#   ProcessingFamily.gamma_infinity / dev_rate_k / induction_t0_min
#       gamma(t) = gamma_inf * (1 - exp(-k*(t - t0))), the Mees-Sheppard law
#       (Glafkides §211). The development points were being interpolated
#       LINEARLY between sparse rows, which overstates gamma mid-bracket by
#       about 4 % and worst exactly where sheets are thinnest. It also
#       supplies the first hard clamp on push processing this project has
#       ever had: usable contrast tops out near 0.80 * gamma_infinity.
#   ProcessingFamily.temp_q10
#       time-temperature compensation, PER FAMILY because the two families
#       disagree -- 2.378 for B&W (doubling per 8 degC) against 2.8-3.5 for
#       colour reversal. Recorded as a conflict, not averaged (method rule 4).
#   ReciprocitySpec.kron_a / kron_log_i0_rel / short_onset_s
#       P = I*t*10^(-a*w), w = sqrt(1 + log10(I/I0)^2), a ~ 0.2
#       (Glafkides §216). Schwarzschild's single exponent is wrong at BOTH
#       ends -- it predicts unbounded loss at long times and unbounded GAIN at
#       short ones. Kron's form has the right asymptotes, and its
#       low-intensity limit p = 1/(1+a) = 0.8333 independently reproduces the
#       p ~ 0.85 the same book quotes from direct measurement. Two numbers
#       from different pages agreeing to 2 % is the strongest internal
#       cross-check in the harvest.
#   MTFSpec.turbidity_gamma_um
#       d = d0 + Gamma*log10(E), Gamma = 0/7/11/18/48 um per DECADE by
#       material class (Glafkides §§240-241, after Selwyn). ⚠ EVERY SPREAD
#       FUNCTION IN THIS PIPELINE IS EXPOSURE-INVARIANT AND THE EMULSION'S IS
#       NOT: on a fast negative a highlight three decades up spreads 54 um
#       wider than a shadow. That is roughly 2 lp/mm of f50 across the tone
#       scale and it is the physical reason a photographic highlight blooms in
#       a way a whole-frame Gaussian cannot reproduce.
#   EmulsionSpec.antihalation / antihalation_undercoat_um
#       ⚠ THE FIELD THAT EXPLAINS AN EXISTING DEFECT RATHER THAN ADDING A
#       NUMBER. `HalationSpec.gain_r` is set on all 184 stocks and not one has
#       a document behind it -- the largest wholly-estimated field in the
#       schema. Glafkides §§402-404 supplies the missing variable: halation
#       onset is 80x threshold on an unprotected support and above 3000x with
#       an absorbing layer, a 37.5x split (6.32 against 11.55 stops) decided
#       by the CONSTRUCTION and nothing else. It is also the field
#       CINESTILL_800T has needed since v17: that stock is VISION3 500T with
#       the rem-jet stripped, so identical emulsion, identical `designation`,
#       famously different halation, and until now the difference lived in a
#       hand-tuned scalar with a prose comment.
#   InterimageSpec.interimage_gamma_ratio_r/g/b
#       ⚠ THIS RECORD'S OWN DOCSTRING SAYS ITS SIX COEFFICIENTS ARE "reasoned
#       ... not measured" AND NAMES THE MISSING QUANTITY. The harvest found it
#       printed: neutral gamma over separation gamma, per record. US6531271
#       gives 0.90-1.05 as a scanning-oriented design band; EP0608959B1
#       measures the print-oriented case an order of magnitude stronger.
#       ⚠ THE TWO SOURCES QUOTE THE RATIO THE OPPOSITE WAY UP; this field is
#       always neutral-over-separation and `validate` refuses anything above
#       1.05 with the reciprocal in the message.
#   AgingSpec.dye_fade_low_density_factor
#       fade is worse in the shadows. US5104782 is the only document in the
#       corpus that ran its light-fade test at two initial densities on every
#       sample, and 68 % residual from D 1.0 against 50 % from D 0.5 means
#       fade LOWERS CONTRAST, which a uniform fraction cannot produce.
#   CoatingSpec.silver_g_per_m2 / gelatin_g_per_m2
#       the most abundant number class in the patent corpus -- seventeen
#       complete layer build-ups -- plus Glafkides' per-class figures and the
#       covering-power constant (1 g Ag/m2 develops to about D 1.0) that
#       turns a total into a checkable bound on Dmax.
#       ⚠ THE PER-LAYER ARRAY WAS PROPOSED AND DELIBERATELY REFUSED: nothing
#       in the 27 stages reads a coating weight, and `gel_silver_ratio` is
#       derived rather than stored because a derivable copy can disagree with
#       its own inputs.
#   ReseauSpec.angle_deg
#       Dufaycolor's reseau runs at 27 degrees on the negative and 45 on the
#       positive, and Glafkides Vol. 2 §475 says why: two regular grids at the
#       same angle beat against each other, so the angles differ ON PURPOSE.
#       The renderer has been laying it out axis-aligned, which is the one
#       angle guaranteed to produce the moire the maker engineered around.
#
# WHAT WAS PROPOSED AND REFUSED, recorded because the refusals are the part a
# later reader will want to re-litigate: per-layer `layer_stack[]` coating
# arrays (nothing reads them); `tabularity_T` (algebraically redundant with
# aspect_ratio and grain_um); `total_coated_silver_g_m2` as a separate field
# (superseded by CoatingSpec); `gel_silver_ratio` (derivable);
# `coupler_solvent_class` (well quantified, -1.7 % to -38 % of gamma, but no
# stock's oil phase is knowable so it could never be populated);
# `curve_polarity` (`StockKind` already carries it); `paper_surface` and
# `paper_grade` (the database contains no paper stock, so about 45 % of this
# harvest describes a material class with no target here and is kept for its
# general models only); and a Callier `Q(gamma)` field, because
# `_callier_beta_for` ALREADY derives Q from the stock's own mid slope --
# Stricker's measured table is therefore wired in as a cross-check
# (G-STRICKER) and not as a new carrier.
#
# ⚠ TWO CONFLICTS ARE RECORDED OPEN AND MUST NOT BE READ AS SETTLED:
#   the GOST speed criterion (Glafkides gives fog+0.2 with S = 1/E; ГОСТ
#   9160-91 and RU2172512C1's own Table 3 column head give fog+0.85), which
#   bears on 18 Soviet stocks; and the magenta light-stability rank, which
#   INVERTS between the 1950s and the 1980s coupler chemistries -- so
#   `dye_fade_m` cannot have a single era-independent default.
