#: DERIVED per-parameter provenance for the parameters `FilmActiveProfiles.md`
#: actually PRINTS (schema v18, generated 2026-08-27, task EM-A6).
#:
#: ⚠ THIS DICT IS A DIFFERENT KIND OF THING FROM `_PARAM_SOURCES` ABOVE AND IS
#: KEPT SEPARATE FOR THAT REASON. The entries above are hand-written: each one
#: is a specific document read by a person, with the bias and the caveats that
#: reading turned up. The entries below are DERIVED BY UNIFORM RULE from
#: registries that already exist in this file -- `mtf_measured`,
#: `provenance.fitted_from`, `_VENDOR_TRACED_CURVES`,
#: `_KODAK_STILL_HARVEST_CURVES`, `_DMIN_LADDER`, `spectral.log_s_g`,
#: `_RESOLVING_POWER`, `_FILMLABPRO_HALATION_IMPORT` -- and they are only as
#: good as those rules. Merging them into one literal would hide which is
#: which; a hand entry always wins and is never displaced by a derived one.
#:
#: WHY IT EXISTS. On 2026-08-27 an audit of `FilmActiveProfiles.md` found 22
#: cells reporting "documented" for a value that was an estimate, because
#: provenance was per-PROFILE and the document fell back to a text-proximity
#: scan of nearby comments -- a scan that a citation mentioning the word
#: "granularity" could fool. `ParamSource` fixed the representation; this dict
#: fixes the COVERAGE, for exactly the columns that document prints. Every cell
#: in those columns is now backed by a record that either names evidence or
#: says plainly that there is none.
#:
#: ⚠ AN 'estimated' OR 'assumed' ENTRY HERE IS A FINDING, NOT A GAP. It is the
#: statement "we looked, and this number is ours" -- which is precisely what
#: the audit found missing. 814 estimated + 329 assumed against 207 traced,
#: 48 derived and 13 stated is an honest census of a database built largely
#: from published curves and class heuristics, not an admission of failure.
#:
#: REGENERATE, do not hand-edit: the rules live in the task EM-A6 generator and
#: re-running it against a changed database is how this stays true. To pin one
#: parameter with real evidence, add it to `_PARAM_SOURCES` above instead --
#: the merge below will leave the derived entry out.
