            conditions='green record, softplus fit; see ToneCurve.is_degenerate before reading gamma as a slope',
            source="Rens, J. E. / Van Bets, K., «Gevachrome-Farbumkehrfilme fuer Farbfernsehen», KINO-TECHNIK 1968 Nr. 10, printed pp. 260 / 262 / 264 / 266. ⚠ IMAGE-ONLY SCAN, NO TEXT LAYER (pdftotext yields 4 bytes), JPEG colour at 150 ppi with ink bleed-through from the reverse of the sheet; every value below was read from the page IMAGES. Only the recto pages are in the scan -- 261/263/265 are absent. Authors: 'Dipl.-Ing. Josef Emiel Rens ist Leiter der Abteilung Marketing-Kine-Produkte, Techn.-Ing. Karel Van Bets technischer Sachbearbeiter fuer Umkehrfarbfilme der Agfa-Gevaert AG in Mortsel, Belgien'. PRINTED AND ADOPTED: Tab. II p262 exposure indices -- 'Kunstlicht 3200-3400 K... 18 DIN (50 ASA)' and 'Tageslicht und Bogenlampen 5500-6500 K, Filter CTO 12: 15 DIN (25 ASA)' (the daylight index is a FILTER-DERIVED figure and, per the treatment already applied to the Kodak and Konica stocks, is deliberately NOT stored as a second film speed); Bilder 5a/5b caption p264 per-layer gammas 'c Gelbschicht gamma 1,25, b Purpurschicht gamma 1,25, a Blaugruenschicht gamma 1,45'; Tab. I p262 the nine-layer coating order including a MAGENTA (Purpur) filter layer as well as the yellow one; 'Farbgleichgewicht der Filme ist auf moderne Projektionslichtquellen mit einer Farbtemperatur von 5000 bis 6000 K abgestimmt'; the conversion-filter cost 'um etwa 3 DIN (eine Blende)'; the interimage statement p264, pronounced in the red-sensitive layer, weaker in green, 'ueberhaupt nicht' in blue. TRACED off Bild 5a's own gridlines (94.0 px per D, 92.5 px per decade): the lower curve pair runs D 2.20 at lg i*t 0.1 -> 1.00 -> 0.26 -> 0.09 at 2.9, fixing dmin at 0.09-0.12. ⚠ DMAX IS NOT DETERMINED: the curves are still climbing at the plot's left edge, so 2.2 is a measured LOWER BOUND and the stored shoulder comes from GEVACHROME_902 [T2 transfer]. ⚠ THE THREE LAYER CURVES CANNOT BE SEPARATED at this scan resolution -- they lie within 1-2 px over most of their length and coincide at the right end -- which is consistent with the paper printing the SAME gamma 1,25 for two of them. NOT PRINTED ANYWHERE: granularity of any kind, resolving power, Dmax, reciprocity, base thickness. Full process on file: Tab. IV 12 steps at 21 C / 25 C plus formulae and pH for GP 110, GP 332, GP 26, GP 308, GP 446, GP 660 (pp264-266); recommended copy stock Gevachrome Print Typ 9.02; storage below 14 C short term, below 4 C long term. Queue G2 holds the untraced MTF (Bild 1a-c, p260) and spectral-sensitivity (Bild 2a/2b, p262) curves",
