                'Table 4 gives 1.2-1.6. So the evidence is: two bands that contain 1.4, 1.5 and 1.6 '
                'alike, and two stock-specific point values that DISAGREE -- Chibisov 1.6 against Iofis '
                '1.4. \u26a0 THE STORED 1.500 SITS BETWEEN THEM AND IS KEPT. Adopting 1.4 would be '
                'picking the newest source found rather than the best one, which is exactly what method '
                'rule 4 forbids; the conflict is recorded instead of averaged. Note 1.4 is also the '
                'midpoint of the GOST band, so it is not a weak reading -- it is a genuine disagreement '
                'with Chibisov, and only a measured wedge would settle it. \u26a0 NEW DATUM THE SCHEMA '
                'CANNOT HOLD: the same table prints speed on TWO illuminants, 45 GOST daylight and 32 '
                'GOST tungsten. `exposure_index` is a single scalar, so the tungsten figure lives here '
                'and nowhere else. Resolving power >= 85 lin/mm is also printed; it is NOT mtf.f50 '
