# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⚠ NOT A CLASS DEFAULT, AND DELIBERATELY NOT ONE. `EmulsionSpec.antihalation`
# is the causal field behind `HalationSpec.threshold_stops`, and Glafkides
# §§402-404 makes the difference between two constructions 37.5x -- 6.32
# stops against 11.55. A wrong construction is therefore not a small error,
# so every entry below is a statement in THIS PROFILE'S OWN provenance
# strings, quoted in the citation, and the ~156 stocks whose records say
# nothing keep "" -- which the field documents as silence and which must
# never be read as "none".
#
# ⚠ THE ONE CONSTRUCTION THIS VOCABULARY CANNOT EXPRESS, recorded because it
# is a real datum being dropped: KODAK_VISION3_200T_5213's sheet states "An
# Anti-halation undercoat replaces the traditional remjet backing layer", and
# KODAK_VISION3_250D_5207's states "acetate safety base with NO rem-jet".
# Kodak's AHU is a DYED undercoat on the emulsion side; `_ANTIHALATIONS`
# offers "colloidal_ag" (specifically colloidal SILVER, and specifically a
# reversal construction because it needs a bleach step) and "dyed_backing"
# (specifically on the BASE side). Neither is what the sheet describes, and
# choosing one would assert a chemistry or a position the sheet does not.
# Both stocks therefore keep "" and the fact stays in their provenance
# strings, where it already is. The enum wants a sixth value, "dyed_undercoat".
#
# Values are (construction, undercoat_um, citation).
