# been laying its grid out axis-aligned -- the one angle guaranteed to
# produce the moire Dufay engineered around by ruling the camera and print
# grids at DIFFERENT angles.
#
# ⚠ "NEGATIVE RESEAU" MEANS THE CAMERA RESEAU. DUFAYCOLOR_1937 is
# `StockKind.REVERSAL` in this database, which is correct -- Dufaycolor 35 mm
# was a reversal-processed camera film -- and it is still the CAMERA stock, so
# it takes the camera grid's 27 degrees. The 45 degrees belongs to the
# separately ruled PRINT reseau, and no print stock in this database carries a
# reseau, so 45 has no target here.
_V29_RESEAU_ANGLE_DEG: dict[str, tuple[float, str]] = {
    "DUFAYCOLOR_1937": (27.0,
        _V29_GLAF2 + ", §497, p.552 -- Dufaycolor's reseau runs at 27 degrees "
        "on the camera (negative) stock and 45 degrees on the positive, and "
        "the angles differ ON PURPOSE: two regular grids laid over one "
        "another at the same angle beat against each other, so the print "
        "grid is deliberately set at a different angle to kill the moire. "
        "⚠ SECTION NUMBER RECORDED BOTH WAYS AND NOT RECONCILED: the "
        "schema-v29 field note cites Vol. 2 §475 for the same statement "
        "while the harvest records it at §497, p.552. Both are kept; neither "
        "is averaged away. ⚠ 27 degrees IS THE CAMERA GRID. This profile is "
        "a camera stock (reversal-processed), so 27 is its angle; 45 belongs "
        "to the print reseau, which no stock in this database carries."),
}

