# ⚠ THE OTHER §A LAYER-RESOLVING ROWS ARE HELD BACK ON PURPOSE. Glafkides
# §509 also prints 120/40/30 for Gevacolor, 120/45/32 for Ferraniacolor
# negative 82 and 80/33/27 for the Agfacolor negative types. Writing those
# needs a LAYER ORDER, and `LayerStack`'s own docstring records that six
# films in the period literature stack their layers unconventionally
# (Duponcolor 275 and Telcolor blue/red/green from the top, Eastmancolor
# positive 5382 blue at the bottom). No source in this corpus states the
# order for Gevacolor, Ferraniacolor or the Agfacolor negative types, and
# `LayerStack.validate` correctly refuses per-layer numbers without one,
# because an assumed order silently asserts a stacking the film may not
# have. Held back, not lost.

# ---- MTFSpec.resolving_power_lp_mm_lowc / _highc -------------------------
# ⚠⚠ THE HARVEST PLAN SAYS THESE "MAP CLEANLY ONTO THE EXISTING
# resolving_power_lp_mm_lowc / _highc PAIR" AND THAT IS WRONG. It is the one
# instruction in §A/§B2 this pass declines outright, and the reason is a
# category error rather than a judgement call:
#
#   * THIS SCHEMA'S PAIR IS A TEST-OBJECT-CONTRAST PAIR. The field docstrings
#     say so: `_lowc` is the datasheet figure at 1.6:1 TOC and `_highc` the
#     figure at 1000:1 TOC. One emulsion, one lens, two subject contrasts.
#   * GLAFKIDES' PAIR IS A LENS-QUALITY PAIR. §233, p.238 (Perrin & Hoadley)
#     tabulates each film through an ORDINARY FUESS LENS and through an
#     APOCHROMAT 1381 -- Super XX 50/95, Panatomic-X 65/105, Tri-X 40/70.
#     One subject contrast, two taking lenses.
#
# The two axes are not the same quantity and a number from one cannot be
# stored in the other's slot. Worse, three of the five named stocks ALREADY
# CARRY a manufacturer-published figure in `_highc` -- Super XX 55 lines/mm
# in SD-21 from the Eastman 1942 «Motion Picture Films» book, Panatomic-X
# sheet 100 and Tri-X sheet 65 lines/mm at 30:1 from the Kodak «Kodak Films»
# Data Book, Fifth Edition (1952) -- and rule 1 forbids replacing a published
# per-stock value with a class or cross-axis one. Glafkides' 95 / 105 / 70
# are recorded here beside them as a THIRD convention (and the disagreement
# with 55 / 100 / 65 is itself the finding: a published resolving power is
# meaningless without its test-object contrast AND its taking lens).
# EASTMAN_TRI_X_5223 has neither slot filled, but Glafkides writes "Tri-X"
# with no format code, so binding his 70/40 to the 1950s cine coating is
# INTERPRETED on top of the axis mismatch -- two unresolved problems, so
# nothing is written. The right home for this table is a new lens-regime
# pair, not this one.

