# writing a processed-film dimension change into it needs saying out loud:
# the figure below is what the film measures the moment it comes off the
# processor, and it is stored here because `shrinkage_pct` is documented as
# "base shrinkage, percent -- drives registration and focus problems in real
# transports", which is exactly what it does. Every storage-related field on
# the record stays zero, so the profile is still fresh in the sense the
# struct means.
#
# ⚠ THE CLASS DEFAULTS ARE DELIBERATELY NOT APPLIED. The same table gives
# 0.06 % for negatives, 0.05 % for B&W positives and 0.07 % for Eastman
# colour prints, which would touch 140 profiles. Writing them would take the
# whole database out of the all-zero state the struct's own docstring rests
# on, for a quantity that no stage reads, on the strength of a class row
